Metadata: {"concept":"A pink adult flamingo bends its curved neck toward a small gray chick nestled beside its legs, making their surprising color contrast part of one intimate natural scene. The article explains how food produces the pink color.","primary_subject":"pink_flamingo_with_gray_chick","secondary_subjects":["gray_flamingo_chick"],"visual_keywords":["pink_flamingo","gray_chick","curved_neck","gentle_encounter"],"composition_hints":["single_connected_natural_scene","adult_bends_toward_chick","optically_centered_motif","no_sequence_or_equation"],"scene_type":"interaction","mood":"contemplative","palette":"teal_amber"}
Selected scene: One coral-pink adult flamingo bends its long graceful S-shaped neck down toward one small fluffy gray chick tucked close beside its legs. Their beaks almost meet in a gentle curious encounter. Compose them as one connected, expressive silhouette, not two display specimens. Pink and gray color contrast carries the intrigue. No arrows, no food or shrimp, no floating ingredients, no stages, no before-and-after panels, no feeding action. Minimal coral, warm gray and muted teal accents, broad flat shapes, no feather texture, no scenery. Transparent background and balanced margins.

